  "details": "VRChat Version:\nVRCSDK3-WORLD-2020.12.09.04.44_Public\n(VRChat version shouldn't matter, this one happens when running in Unity Editor as well)\nDescription of the bug:\n\nI use UI buttons in my world and for some of them I just create list of actions for the \"On Click()\" event in the unity editor. Some of the buttons stopped working after some update a few months ago - now when I click them nothing happens. I noticed in the console that I get errors such as this:\n\"Events on 'Turnonbutton' were removed because one of them targeted a prohibited type 'Camera', method 'set_enabled' or object 'Camera (1)'.\"\nThis is because one of the actions is to enable Camera component on one of the GameObjects. Similarily, there's an error for MeshRenderer.set_material action. I'm not sure why some Components are \"prohibited\" in events but they were working fine before.\n\n\nSteps to reproduce (how did you encounter the bug?):\n1. Create an object with Camera component\n2. Create an UI button\n3. Add an action in the button's \"On Click()\" event, select object with camera and action to Camera.enabled\n4. Run the world and try to click the button",
